<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Artvin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Artvin is a city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, the capital of Artvin Province, on the Çoruh river near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> and the Georgian border. Part of the medieval Georgian lands of Tao-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klarjeti">Klarjeti</a>, it passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> in the 16th century and was annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1878. It returned to Turkey under the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a> in 1921.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/artvin.jpg" alt="Artvin" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cagriaksu25 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A%C3%87%C3%9C_%C5%9Eehir_Yerle%C5%9Fkesi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
